## Run 3: fetches stopped on all second replicas (s1r2, s2r2, s3r2)
A) writer in_order + prefer_localhost_replica=0 from s1r1; reader in_order, prefer_localhost_replica=1 (default) from s2r2
   RETRY(395); RETRY(395); PASS visible=193  <-- stale pass (reader read its own lagging local replica)
B) same, reader prefer_localhost_replica=0
   PASS 300; PASS 300; PASS 300
C) writer default from s2r2; reader in_order + prefer_localhost_replica=0 from s1r1
   PASS 300; PASS 300; PASS 300

## Run 4: recovery window: s2r1 stopped, batch written (shard 2 -> s2r2), s2r1 restarted with fetches frozen
reader in_order + prefer_localhost_replica=0: visible 300 (both checks). The recovered replica was not chosen
immediately; inferred cause: load balancing ranks replicas by recent error count (distributed_replica_error_half_life=60s).
